Chapter: Identity
  cites Foreword chapter Ed25519
  cites Foreword chapter HeapScrub
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 To authenticate gives a Text credential token: the active identity,
 but only while the private key is unlocked (key-status), and the empty
 string otherwise. A non-empty answer is therefore proof that the key
 is loaded -- the machine's authentication gate. Signing with the loaded
 key is key-sign-bytes below (2026-08-19); a signed credential token
 over it is not built.

 We say:

Section: Effect

  effect Identity where

Section: Operations

  current-user : [Identity] Text
  current-user =
    if identity-whoami 0 == 0 then ""
    else "id:" & show (identity-whoami 0)

  authenticate : [Identity] Text
  authenticate =
    if key-status == 1 then current-user
    else ""

Section: Signing With The Loaded Key

 30608 is `identity-key-addr` in the emitter's X86_64Boot: the 32 bytes
 key-load (syscall 15) copies the seed into and key-zero (syscall 16)
 clears; 30640 beside it is the loaded flag key-status reads. The address
 is the kernel's and is repeated here as a number because the foreword
 cannot cite the compiler.

  identity-key-slot : Integer = 30608
  identity-key-slot-len : Integer = 32
  identity-sig-len : Integer = 64

  key-slot-bytes : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  key-slot-bytes (i) (acc) =
    if i >= identity-key-slot-len then acc
    else key-slot-bytes (i + 1) (list-push acc (peek-byte identity-key-slot i))

  key-zero-fill : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  key-zero-fill (n) (acc) =
    if n <= 0 then acc else key-zero-fill (n - 1) (list-push acc 0)

  key-copy-into : List Integer, List Integer, Integer -> Integer
  key-copy-into (dst) (src) (i) =
    if i >= list-length src then 0
    else let w = list-set-at dst i (list-at src i)
    in key-copy-into dst src (i + 1)

  key-public : [Identity] Maybe (List Integer)
  key-public =
    if key-status /= 1 then None
    else let out = key-zero-fill identity-key-slot-len []
    in let mark = __heap-save
    in let pub = ed25519-public-key (key-slot-bytes 0 [])
    in let c = key-copy-into out pub 0
    in let s = heap-scrub-to mark
    in Just out

  key-sign-bytes : List Integer -> [Identity] Maybe (List Integer)
  key-sign-bytes (msg) =
    if key-status /= 1 then None
    else let out = key-zero-fill identity-sig-len []
    in let mark = __heap-save
    in let seed = key-slot-bytes 0 []
    in let sig = ed25519-sign seed (ed25519-public-key seed) msg
    in let c = key-copy-into out sig 0
    in let s = heap-scrub-to mark
    in Just out
